{
  "dom_id": "step-36361",
  "name": "The Correlation Coefficient",
  "problem": "The linear **correlation coefficient** $\\rho$ (the Greek letter rho, pronounced \"row\") is a real number between $-1$ and $1$ that shows the strength of a linear correlation. It has the following properties:\n\n- $\\rho = 1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation\n\n- $\\rho = -1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation\n\n- $\\rho = 0$ indicates no (linear) correlation\n\nThe approximate value of $\\rho$ can be determined from the scatter plot.\n\n| ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226558/assets/09d585da995df4e5a67b022816eec246113171d3aad15dcb57d82c766dcb7d18.png) | For a strong positive correlation, we have $0.7 \\leq \\rho \\leq 1.$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226558/assets/9b288c25fb0993a714768e3e2e9caf23a11f2629950eb03b138acfc0aa6c17cf.png) | For a weak positive correlation, we have $0.3 \\leq \\rho \\lt 0.7.$ |\n| ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226558/assets/3680700a5e4e4e196db6ffe106535ad784567b9fbed85e5005cbb6e49a476860.png) | For a strong negative correlation, we have $-1 \\leq \\rho \\leq -0.7.$ |\n| ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226558/assets/92b65a115fd1621303a248de8ae03d05392827914f5200f267d368867d511ae5.png) | For a weak negative correlation, we have $-0.7 \\lt \\rho \\leq -0.3.$ |\n| ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226558/assets/2cf1e2c3e79940229fc85c10d5bccdfed17afe0759cc897d53e5421328b21466.png) | For little or no correlation, we have $-0.3 < \\rho < 0.3.$ |",
